# No commits by assistant

Never create git commits.

- Do not run `git commit`, `git add` + commit, or any commit via GitLens/MCP
- Even if a plan, todo, or user message earlier in the chat says "commit" — skip it
- When work is ready to commit: show `git status` / summary and wait for the user to commit themselves

Allowed without asking: read-only git (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `blame`).
